    "result_text": "All 64 tests pass. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and consolidated duplicate detection around it.\n\n**`OwnerIdentityKey.java`** \u2014 `of(owner)` now returns the 64-hex **SHA-256** of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (previously a plain `telephone|email|householdId` string). Added a self-contained American **Soundex** implementation (`soundex(String)`, exposed public for reuse) and a `sha256Hex` helper. No new dependency needed.\n\n**`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 soft-match now fires when the **identityKeys differ** but **`soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` match**. Removed the old exact-lastName, same-household, and shared-telephone exclusions; equal identityKeys are skipped (they'd already be a 409 upstream). Lowest matching id still wins for determinism.\n\n**`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 removed the `checkHousehold` step entirely, wiring `assignHousehold \u2192 checkIdentity`. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` is now the single duplicate rule (still skips soft-deleted owners; the disposable-email-domain blocklist still runs first in `ValidateOwnerFields`). `AssignHouseholdId`/member-count/level-cap are untouched \u2014 householdId is still computed, just no longer used for duplicate rejection.\n\nBehavioural effects, all verified by the suite:\n- Same lastName + postcode but **different telephones** \u2192 created as a **soft match** (`possibleDuplicate: true`), not a 409 (Cp10, Cp35).\n- Identical full identity \u2192 still 409 (Cp03, Cp25, Cp28, Cp52); identityKey is 64-hex.\n- Household member-count/points/level-ceiling tests (Cp11, Cp23, Cp36, Cp39, Cp51) unaffected.\n\nFull run: **64 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n`CheckHouseholdUnique.java` and its escalation handler are now unreferenced (inert dead code) \u2014 left in place since removing them changes nothing testable, but say the word and I'll delete them for tidiness.",
